{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable events) from motion commands (controllable events). The specification automata encode the safe, conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are triggered by obstacle events. Recovery states deterministically select a single turn direction based on which side is blocked, and full_rotate is reserved for deadlock/blocked situations only. The design ensures safety, avoids oscillation, and maximizes coverage progress.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion: G1 for perception, G2 for motion commands.",
    "Specification automata E1 (main policy) binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing deterministic recovery and exploration alternation."
  ],
